orthant 1 language

- # `↯/s.24.1` — `recover` argument must be match cases
+ # `↯/s.24.1` — l'argument de `recover` doit être une série de cas

- Raised at compiletime when the argument to `recover` is not written as a literal block of
- `case` clauses.
+ Levée à la compilation lorsque l'argument de `recover` n'est pas écrit comme un bloc littéral de
+ clauses `case`.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- `recover` inspects the cases as the code compiles, so that it knows which error types are
- handled. A partial function computed elsewhere, or passed as a value, cannot be inspected.
+ `recover` inspecte les cas pendant la compilation du code, afin de savoir quels types d'erreurs
+ sont gérés. Une fonction partielle calculée ailleurs, ou passée comme valeur, ne peut pas être
+ inspectée.

- ## Example message
+ ## Exemple de message

=
- ```
+ ```

- [↯/s.24.1] argument to `recover` should be a partial function implemented as match cases
+ [↯/s.24.1] argument to `recover` should be a partial function implemented as match cases

= [↯/s.24.1] argument to `recover` should be a partial function implemented as match cases
- ```
+ ```

- ## Resolution
+ ## Résolution

- Write the cases inline:
+ Écrivez les cas en ligne :

- ```scala
+ ```scala

- def readConfiguration(): Text raises Io.Error = t"verbose = true"
+ def readConfiguration(): Text raises Io.Error = t"verbose = true"

- val fallback: Text = t""
+ val fallback: Text = t""

- recover:
+ recover:

-   case error: Io.Error => fallback
+   case error: Io.Error => fallback

- . protect(readConfiguration())
+ . protect(readConfiguration())

= . protect(readConfiguration())
- ```
+ ```

